[32m+[m[32m## 2026-09-02 — musaibbhat120605[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Fixed[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Downloaded songs missing from the Downloads screen after reinstalling the app.**[m
[32m+[m[32m  The files were never actually lost — `syncDownloadsFromStorage()` (which[m
[32m+[m[32m  re-discovers tracks in the public `LastWave` folder after the app's[m
[32m+[m[32m  database is wiped, e.g. by a reinstall) was silently finding nothing on[m
[32m+[m[32m  Android 13+. The app targets SDK 35, `READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` is correctly[m
[32m+[m[32m  capped at `maxSdkVersion="32"` for that target, but the replacement[m
[32m+[m[32m  permission for API 33+, `READ_MEDIA_AUDIO`, was never declared — and the[m
[32m+[m[32m  app had **no runtime permission-request code at all** for either[m
[32m+[m[32m  permission, on any Android version. Without it, the OS returns an empty[m
[32m+[m[32m  directory listing rather than an error, so the scan always came back[m
[32m+[m[32m  empty and the screen looked like the downloads were gone.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m  - Declared `READ_MEDIA_AUDIO` in the manifest.[m
[32m+[m[32m  - `MainActivity` now requests the correct runtime permission on launch[m
[32m+[m[32m    (`READ_MEDIA_AUDIO` on API 33+, `READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE` below that),[m
[32m+[m[32m    mirroring the existing `POST_NOTIFICATIONS` request pattern.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m  Once granted, reopening the Downloads screen re-runs[m
[32m+[m[32m  `syncDownloadsFromStorage()` and repopulates the list from the files[m
[32m+[m[32m  already on disk — no re-downloading needed.[m
[32m+[m
